{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A placeholder is often the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"only"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" thing on screen for a few hundred milliseconds, or the only thing a user with a slow connection sees for much longer than that — so it’s worth it being as accessible as the real content it stands in for. The default ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenStateDefault{Empty,Loading,Error}View","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"UIView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s handle all of this out of the box; this article rounds up what they do and how a fully custom placeholder can match them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"VoiceOver-announcements","text":"VoiceOver announcements","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each default placeholder announces its own appearance — "},{"code":"AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(_:).post()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in SwiftUI, "},{"code":"UIAccessibility.post(notification:.announcement, argument:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in UIKit — so a screen settling into ","type":"text"},{"code":".empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is heard, not just seen.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","type":"reference"},{"text":" exposes that same wording for any case, so a fully custom placeholder can announce transitions consistently instead of inventing its own text:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".onAppear {","    if let announcement = state.accessibilityAnnouncement {","        AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(announcement).post()","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"text":" — your own content is what VoiceOver should read at that point — and, for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"text":", it’s the default “Nothing Here” text; announce your own custom title directly instead if your placeholder shows one, so VoiceOver matches what’s on screen. See ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","isActive":true},{"text":" for the full examples.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Reduce-Motion","type":"heading","text":"Reduce Motion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The default Loading placeholder’s ring spins via a repeating rotation animation — purely decorative, and exactly the kind of large, continuous motion Reduce Motion exists to suppress. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView"},{"text":" reads SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessibilityReduceMotion"},{"text":" environment value; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView"},{"text":" reads ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.isReduceMotionEnabled"},{"text":" and also observes ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIAccessibility.reduceMotionStatusDidChangeNotification","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so an already-visible spinner responds immediately if the setting changes while on screen, not just on the next appearance. Either way, the ring stays static — still colorful, just not spinning — instead of disabling itself entirely, since a static ring still communicates “loading” on its own."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Increase-Contrast","text":"Increase Contrast","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All three default placeholders’ gradient icons\/ring respect Increase Contrast — SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorSchemeContrast"},{"text":" environment value, UIKit’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAccessibility.isDarkerSystemColorsEnabled"},{"text":" (observed live the same way Reduce Motion is). A multi-stop gradient can dip below an acceptable contrast ratio in places a single flat color never does, so when Increase Contrast is on, every gradient is swapped for a solid ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".label"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".primary"},{"text":" tint instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Dynamic-Type","text":"Dynamic Type","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Empty\/Error placeholders’ text scales with Dynamic Type: SwiftUI’s "},{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"ErrorView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" get this for free from "},{"code":"ContentUnavailableView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own text styles, and "},{"code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyUIView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"ErrorUIView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s labels use "},{"code":"UIFont.preferredFont(forTextStyle: .body, compatibleWith:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Both are covered up to the largest accessibility size by snapshot tests, so a regression that silently pins the text to a fixed size would be caught. The default Loading placeholder has no text at all — its ring is a fixed-size shape, unaffected by Dynamic Type by design."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Identifiers-for-XCUITest","text":"Identifiers for XCUITest","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every default placeholder exposes a stable "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accessibilityIdentifier"},{"type":"text","text":", independent of any localized or custom text, so a UI test can assert which state is showing without string-matching:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Identifier","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Shown on","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"screenStates.loading","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"screenStates.empty","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultEmptyUIView"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"screenStates.error","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorUIView","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.error.retryButton"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Retry button, when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"text":" is given","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screenStates.error.secondaryActionButton"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The secondary action button, when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"secondaryAction"},{"type":"text","text":" is given"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"},"abstract":[{"text":"Everything the default placeholders — and your own custom ones — get for free: VoiceOver, Reduce Motion, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type, and stable identifiers for XCUITest.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/accessibility"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"title":"Accessibility"},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithUIKit":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drive a UIKit screen’s four states with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates